worked_examples.solution:
(a) Zinc, $\mathrm{Zn^{2+}}$ (white precipitate dissolving in excess sodium hydroxide). (b) The flame test only identifies lithium, sodium, potassium and copper(II);

a negative (no useful colour) result is consistent with zinc and does not contradict it, since zinc was never expected to give a flame colour.

(c) An anion test from the previous lesson (for example, the chloride or sulfate test) would identify the anion and complete the compound's full identification.
